/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 236.0 Tm
() Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 224.0 Tm
(1. Read the site ambient temperature at the trip time from the history. If it) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 212.0 Tm
(was above 95 degF, the cause is external conditions; the machine is not) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 200.0 Tm
(diagnosed before the conditions are corrected.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 188.0 Tm
(2. Read the discharge pressure and the saturated condensing temperature from) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 176.0 Tm
(the trend history for the 15 minutes before the trip.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 164.0 Tm
(3. Check the condenser coil from the ground. Do not climb the unit.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 152.0 Tm
(4. Check the glycol concentration with a refractometer for the inhibitor) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 140.0 Tm
(package, not for ethylene glycol.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 128.0 Tm
(5. Compare the evaporator approach temperature. A large approach with a clean) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 116.0 Tm
(condenser indicates a refrigerant side or a glycol side problem, not a) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 104.0 Tm
(compressor problem.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 92.0 Tm
() Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 80.0 Tm
(Do not reset the unit and leave it. Three F-13 trips in one shift stops the) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 68.0 Tm
(unit until the cause is established.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
1 0 0 1 50 56.0 Tm
